# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# VibeVerse Server Environment Variables
# Copy this file to server/.env and fill in keys
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

# TMDb API Key (FREE — no rate limits on discover/search)
# Get it at: https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api
# Register → Request API → Use "Developer" key (v3 auth)
TMDB_API_KEY=e04853aa5fd407eef838275300f6c430

# YouTube Data API v3 Key (10,000 units/day FREE quota)
# Get it at: https://console.cloud.google.com/
# Steps: New Project → Enable "YouTube Data API v3" → Credentials → API Key
# NOTE: If quota runs out, music section gracefully shows fallback message.
# Solution for quota: Create multiple API keys and rotate them (see note below)
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=AIzaSyBrOT18iL0_NJ2_13Sgoq2qT42pB0SN_mc

# OPTIONAL: Redis for persistent caching (reduces API calls significantly)
# Without Redis, in-memory cache resets on server restart
# Free Redis: https://railway.app or https://upstash.com
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# Server port
PORT=5000

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# YOUTUBE QUOTA NOTE:
# YouTube API gives 10,000 units/day. Each search = 100 units.
# So you get ~100 searches/day before quota hits.
# 
# To avoid quota issues:
# 1. The server caches results for 1 hour (reduces repeat calls)
# 2. Add Redis (see above) to persist cache across restarts
# 3. Create 2-3 Google Cloud projects with separate API keys
#    and rotate YOUTUBE_API_KEY between them
#
# TMDb has NO practical rate limit for normal usage.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────